{
  "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
  "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Edward S. Zas",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Speedy Trial Act protects the public, as well as the personal interests of defendants, by mandating the prompt disposition of Federal criminal prosecutions. In this case, the Government and the district court failed to comply with the clear requirements of the act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about, Mr. Zas, that the court thought it was home free on the Speedy Trial Act? After all, it had gotten a waiver for all time. Isn't that why the 165 days?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: -- I was not talking about the perpetual waiver. I was talking about the waiver for whatever number of days he actually took in -- in that case, which was what? 90 days?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The problem here is that the statute -- the Congress knew that this kind of thing would happen. Defendants would want delay. Defendants would be quite happy to put off their trial for as long as they could."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Maybe you could say then that it's the Government that has the right. If it's the Government that has the right, then Government should have objected."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, it gives defendants every reason to delay in hopes of manufacturing a speedy trial violation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0002-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The action is dismissed for a Speedy Trial Act violation because the position of the Petitioner here is accepted by this Court and the Government just reindicts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this -- is there a statute of limitations problem in -- in these cases if their dismissal is without prejudice?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Did the Government raise at least the -- the theory of judicial estoppel in the litigation before it reached this point?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Am -- am I correct that the -- the particular provision that you think is relevant here is -- is (h)(1)(A) on page 4 of the -- the appendix in the blue brief?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One of the Court's bedrock principles is that judges are not free to rewrite the statute that Congress has enacted. This statute and the whole statutory scheme here speaks very clearly and very precisely, and it would be unwise, even if permitted, for the Court to start tinkering with it because the whole system will start to unravel if the -- if the requirement of express findings and reasons turns into a could have/would have/should have contest, in which case trial judges will take the act less seriously knowing that the court of appeals could make the findings for them. And it will make the court of appeals' job harder because they'll be guessing after the fact what discretionary decision the trial judge would have made."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Where does the act say that, that there has to be a finding at the time?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2005-05-5992",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "0c25fd3d589538c0c0b7ec8438cbfe62f621250e9a456fe8c2173eacfcc7b739",
      "evidence_id": "ev-0c25fd3d5895-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:02 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    }
  ],
